[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122643"] :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,i+(x+y)^{2}\\,j$\n- $Q(x,y,z)=y\\,i-xy\\,j+(z+1)\\,k$\n- $R(t)=(t+1)\\,i-(3t-1)\\,j$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $R(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186172210 :question/answer-fields 17592186168463] {:db/id "q-122465/selection/ma-v1/d2d3d21f1cb38e3fcbe0303fd40e2c374332303bf66028b2bc8a3209449d2cb2/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "e085e56c-ab04-5255-8f2e-e486bf529732" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122465/selection/ma-v1/d2d3d21f1cb38e3fcbe0303fd40e2c374332303bf66028b2bc8a3209449d2cb2/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "66bb3258-d9ab-5a7a-a63f-c101903168af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122465/selection/ma-v1/d2d3d21f1cb38e3fcbe0303fd40e2c374332303bf66028b2bc8a3209449d2cb2/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8f8a7227-1927-51df-b1cd-eaa236149836" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensur