elds on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $G(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$\n- $H(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{xy}\\,j$\n- $K(x,y,z)=x\\,i-y\\,j+z\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $G(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $H(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122465/selection/ma-v1/d2d3d21f1cb38e3fcbe0303fd40e2c374332303bf66028b2bc8a3209449d2cb2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122653/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "0ff6da96-05a5-532c-85a5-cc5fdf1b92a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122653/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "768a89b8-6647-5a6c-81fa-f88e2a38b2b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122653/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "48ff8ded-4323-51b5-b974-fc471c4b1e9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122653/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2e9c861d-81d5-57f5-9b7f-52d429381913" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122653/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a29c1389-354a-5f37-9781-03b858b563e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122653/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0c08d0d-9def-515c-9953-db6a6492384e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122653/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-122653/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-122653/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-122653/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-122653/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-122653/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122653" :question/id #uuid "04610650-408c-5968-86aa-9a134cc6b4b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122653" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $A(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)⟩$\n- $B(x,y,z)=⟨-2x,3{y}^{3},{z}^{5}⟩$\n- $C(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},{e}^{t-1}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122653/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122653"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122678/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "99d21c19-c99c-5f0b-bfa4-f42943df8126" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122678/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "41ab9b5d-2fd7-5aec-aee0-304e65d2805a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122678/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a11d1381-5cfe-5e01-adb6-d137bf5de30c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122678/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "384a6e96-661d-5b22-bf7a-164e9ab6be82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122678/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "37f7df0e-ae66-5127-9962-f5e0a94d8c74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122678/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4f3a99d-28fc-555f-98b1-b751588c1cb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122678/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-122678/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-122678/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-122678/selection/df67a18079e3b7